General qualifications:<br>
Motivated, self-starter;
Has to possess strong writing skills;
Excellent communication skills;
BA degree;
Superior attention to detail and strong follow-up skills;
Needs to demonstrate a proven ability to work  both collaboratively  on a team and  independently and autonomously;
Should be eager to grow and learn in the position;
Ability to accept and make use of constructive feedback;
Flexibility;
Must be punctual and respect all deadlines;
Self-discipline and strong work ethic;
Ought to possess an ability to work in a busy work environment while remaining attentive to detail;
Must be  able to prioritize, be organized, and meet  all project organizational deadlines.</p>

Requirements specific to the position:<br>
Have an eye for good storytelling and an inherent understanding of grammatical structure;
Be able at times to work independently and in collaboration with printers, publishers and assistant editors when necessary;
Needs to have a minimum of one year professional experience with inEffects, inPrinting, and inPremiere;
Experience with learning management systems, a plus;
Comfortable with different operating systems;
Interest in learning new software and staying current with technological changes in the industry;
Willingness to work long hours as needed to meet delivery deadlines;
Willingness to proofread and make changes as much as  is required.</p>
Duties and responsibilities include:<br>
Editing copy, working  either independently or with an editor, depending on the project;
Preparing project elements, outputs and deliverables;
Screening of quality control materials;
Preparing text for transcription;
Managing text archive.<br><br>
Please send cv to: bobbykpl@BFPPublishing.com
